DTSTAMP:20260802T111854Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Referrals by Out-of-Network Direct Health Car
 e Providers (Supersedes Bulletin 434)
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPA RTMENT O F P R OFES SIO NAL  & FINA NCI
 AL  RE GUL ATIO N  \nBUREAU OF  INSU RAN CE  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOffice
  Location: 76 Northern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 
 34 State House Station\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insuran
 ce \nPhone: (207) 624-8475  TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assi
 stance: (800) 300-5000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \n \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor 
 \nRobert L. Carey \nSuperintendent \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \nBullet
 in 490 \nReferrals by Out-of-Network Direct Health Care Providers \n(Super
 sedes Bulletin 434) \nIn 2019\, the Bureau issued Bulletin 434 to describe
  the requirement for health carriers to honor \nreferrals made by an enrol
 lee’s direct primary care provider\, even if that provider is out of net
 work\, \non the same terms as if the provider had been in the carrier’s 
 network. \nThe purpose of this Bulletin is to update Bulletin 434 to refle
 ct changes to the direct care law \nenacted by the Legislature in 2025\, t
 o include providers who are not primary care providers.1  All \nlicensed p
 hysicians\, and other  advanced health care practitioners who are authoriz
 ed to engage in \nindependent medical practice in Maine\, are now authoriz
 ed to enter into direct health care service \nagreements (DHCSAs) 2 with p
 atients\, and the term “direct primary care provider” has been \nchang
 ed to “direct health care provider” (DHCP) wherever it appears. \nConf
 orming changes have been made to the referral provision of the Health Plan
  Improvement \nAct\, so that it now applies whenever there is a DHCSA betw
 een the enrollee and the referring \nprovider.3  As under the prior law\, 
 the carrier may not deny a referral made by a DHCP\, or impose \nadditiona
 l cost sharing or other conditions on the referred service\, for the sole 
 reason that the \nreferring provider is out of network or that the referri
 ng provider practices on a direct care basis.  \nThe carrier may continue 
 to apply its usual cost sharing requirements\, benefit limitations\, and \
 nreasona\nhttps://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insuranc
 e/files/inline-files/490.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/490.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f180f9edcb8236e2@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260802T111854Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Flexibility Requested for Federal Employees a
 nd other Impacted Persons
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPA RTMENT O F P R OFES SIO NAL  & FINA NCI
 AL  RE GUL ATIO N  \nBUREAU OF  INSU RAN CE  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOffice
  Location: 76 Northern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 
 34 State House Station\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insuran
 ce \nPhone: (207) 624-8475  TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assi
 stance: (800) 300-5000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \n \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor 
 \nRobert L. Carey \nSuperintendent \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \nBullet
 in 488 \nFlexibility Requested for Federal Employees and other Impacted Pe
 rsons \nMany Maine residents are experiencing financial hardship due to th
 e continuing federal \ngovernment shutdown. In response to this disruption
 \, the Bureau requests that all Maine licensed \ninsurance companies be fl
 exible and proactive in working with policyholders who are experiencing \n
 temporary financial hardship due to the shutdown to keep essential insuran
 ce policies in place. \nThis includes federal employees and other persons 
 whose pay has been directly impacted\, such as \npersons whose employment 
 relies upon federal grants and contracts which have been affected by \nthe
  shutdown. Specifically\, the Bureau requests that all insurance companies
  provide these affected \npolicyholders with at least a 60 -day grace peri
 od to pay insurance premiums or other flexible \npayment options so that i
 nsurance policies are not cancelled for nonpayment of premium and \npenalt
 ies are not assessed during this challenging time.  \nThe requested grace 
 period and flexible payment options are intended to be applied to \npremiu
 ms due after the initial premium has been made to secure coverage. They ar
 e not intended \nto change the terms of the issued policy or to be conside
 red a forgiveness of the premium. This \nrequest is directed to all admitt
 ed and non -admitted insurance companies that provide any \ninsurance cove
 rage in Maine including life\, health\, auto\, property\, casualty\, and o
 ther types of \ninsurance. The Bureau  encourages all carriers  \nhttps://
 www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/files/inline-fil
 es/Bulletin%20488.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/Bulletin%20488.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ea0db7fad4bf7f80@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260802T111854Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Network Adequacy Guidance for Plan Year 2026
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPA RTMENT O F P R OFES SIO NAL  & FINA NCI
 AL  RE GUL ATIO N  \nBUREAU OF  INSU RAN CE  \n \nOffice Location: 76 Nort
 hern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 34 State House Sta
 tion\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insurance \nPhone: (207) 
 624-8475 TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assistance: (800) 300-5
 000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor \nRobert L. Carey \nSu
 perintendent \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \nBulletin 487 \nNetwork Adequ
 acy Guidance for Plan Year 2026 \nThe Legislature has approved amendments 
 to Bureau of Insurance Rule Chapter 850 that require \nthe Bureau to estab
 lish new network adequacy standards effective for plan years beginning on 
 or \nafter January 1\, 2026\, and to publish those standards and an except
 ion process in an annual Bureau \nof Insurance bulletin.1  The standards m
 ust equal or exceed the minimum requirements set by the \nCenters for Medi
 care and Medicaid Services (CMS) for qualified health plans  offered on th
 e \nMarketplace.2 \nFor plan years beginning on or after January 1\, 2026\
 , the Superintendent hereby adopts the \nstandards that CMS has adopted fo
 r Medicare Advantage plans in the State of Maine\, as shown in \nthe sprea
 dsheet that is attached as Appendix 1 \, which sets forth maximum distance
  and driving \ntime for primary care and for designated specialty and faci
 lity types\, based on the enrollee’s county \nof residence.  Insurers mu
 st contract with a sufficient number of providers and facilities to ensure
  \nthat at least 90 percent of enrollees in each county can access care wi
 thin the specified travel time \nand distance standards.  Distance and est
 imated driving time  must be measured according to a \nmethodology CMS ref
 ers to as “ geographic distance \,”3 which uses an algorithm designed 
 to \nidentify the most likely driving route\, considering various topograp
 hic factors that consumers \nexperience when traveling to access care. \nI
 nsurers must also continue to meet Rule 850’s requirement to main\nhttps
 ://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/files/inline-
 files/487.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/487.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:1dd266c27a57939a@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260802T111854Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Coverage for Immunizations\, Including Covid-
 19 Vaccines
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPARTMENT OF PROFESSIONAL  & FINANCIAL  REG
 ULATION  \nBUREAU OF  INSURANCE  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOffice Location: 7
 6 Northern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 34 State Hou
 se Station\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insurance \nPhone: 
 (207) 624-8475  TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assistance: (800
 ) 300-5000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \n \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor \nRobert L. 
 Carey \nSuperintendent \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \nBulletin 486 \nCov
 erage for Immunizations\, Including Covid-19 Vaccines \nPursuant to Maine 
 law\, health insurance carriers are required\, at a minimum\, to provide c
 overage \nfor immunizations “that are consistent with the recommendation
 s of the American Academy \nof Pediatrics\, the American Academy of Family
  Physicians or the American Academy \nof Obstetricians and Gynecologists [
 collectively\, the Medical Academies]”  24-A M.R.S. § 4320-\nA(1)(B).  
 This includes coverage for the Covid- 19 vaccine\, when recommended by the
  Medical \nAcademies.  There is also a separate mandate for coverage of an
 y Covid-19 vaccine “licensed or \nauthorized under an emergency use auth
 orization by the United States Food and Drug \nAdministration\,”  24-A M
 .R.S. § 4320-P(3)(A).  These two provisions operate independently\, and \
 neither one\, if it applies\, is sufficient to require the carrier to prov
 ide coverage. \nWhere the Covid -19 vaccine is a mandated coverage under e
 ither of Sections 4320- A(1)(B) or \n4320-P(3)(A)\, Maine law also require
 s carriers to cover the cost of the Covid- 19 vaccine and all \nassociated
  costs of administration\, without cost sharing or prior authorization.\n1
   Carriers may only \nrequire use of their network as a condition for  fir
 st-dollar Covid-19 vaccine coverage if the \nimmunization is available fro
 m a network pharmacy or other network provider with no additional \ndelay.
 2 \nWhen carriers are acting as administrators for self -insured and level
 -funded health benefit plans\, \nthe Superintendent expects carriers to ma
 ke plan \nhttps://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insuranc
 e/files/inline-files/486.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/486.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
